---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import BlogPost from '../components/BlogPost.astro';

const title = "Best Amazon Price Tracking Tools (2026)";
const description = "Compare the best Amazon price tracking tools for sellers in 2026. Real-time alerts, Buy Box protection, and actionable insights compared: Talon, Keepa, CamelCamelCamel, RepricerExpress, SellerSnap.";
---

<Layout title={`${title} — Talon`}>
  <BlogPost
    title={title}
    description={description}
    category="Amazon Seller"
    readTime="6 min read"
    updated="Jan 2026"
  >
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lead">On Amazon, a 5% price drop from a competitor can strip your Buy Box in minutes. A market-wide shift can mean a margin window that closes in hours. The problem is never <em>lack of data</em> — it's knowing <strong>what to do, and when.</strong></p>

      <div class="stat-trio">
        <div class="stat-item">
          <div class="stat-num stat-num-r">82%</div>
          <div class="stat-label">of Amazon sales go through the Buy Box</div>
          <div class="stat-sub">Losing it is losing the sale</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-item">
          <div class="stat-num stat-num-w">&lt;15 min</div>
          <div class="stat-label">How fast competitors react to price changes</div>
          <div class="stat-sub">Manual monitoring can't keep up</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-item">
          <div class="stat-num stat-num-g">+18%</div>
          <div class="stat-label">Average margin left on the table during supply squeezes</div>
          <div class="stat-sub">When sellers don't react in time</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2 id="comparison">Quick comparison</h2>
      <p>Five tools, one table — judged on the metrics that actually matter for active Amazon sellers.</p>

      <div class="comparison-wrap">
        <table class="comparison-table">
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Tool</th><th>Best For</th><th>Real-Time</th><th>Actionable</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="hl">
              <td><span class="tc-icon">🎯</span> Talon <span class="tc-us-chip">This guide</span></td>
              <td>Fast pricing decisions</td>
              <td><span class="check-yes">✓</span></td>
              <td><span class="check-yes">✓</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Keepa</td>
              <td>Historical tracking</td>
              <td><span class="check-no">✗</span></td>
              <td><span class="check-no">✗</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>CamelCamelCamel</td>
              <td>Casual price history</td>
              <td><span class="check-no">✗</span></td>
              <td><span class="check-no">✗</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>RepricerExpress</td>
              <td>Rule-based automation</td>
              <td><span class="check-warn">⚠</span></td>
              <td><span class="check-no">✗</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>SellerSnap</td>
              <td>AI repricing</td>
              <td><span class="check-warn">⚠</span></td>
              <td><span class="check-warn">⚠</span></td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="parasite-section">
        <h3>Best Keepa alternative for real-time decisions</h3>
        <p>Keepa is the go-to for Amazon price history — but it's a research tool, not a decision tool. It shows you what happened, not what to do.</p>
        <p>If you need to react to competitor price changes in real time (not hours later), you need a different approach.</p>
      </div>

      <hr/>

      <h2 id="talon">1. Talon — Best for real-time decisions</h2>
      <div class="tool-card featured">
        <div class="tc-head">
          <div class="tc-head-left">
            <span class="tc-rank">#1 — Editor's Pick</span>
            <div class="tc-name">Talon</div>
            <div class="tc-tagline">Detects price changes and tells you exactly what to do before you lose the sale.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="tc-verdict-wrap">
            <span class="verdict-lbl">Verdict</span>
            <span class="v-badge vb-best">Best Overall</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="tc-content">
          <p class="tc-desc">Talon sits in a different category. While others track prices and surface data, Talon answers: <strong>what should I do right now, and how much is it costing me?</strong> Every alert includes estimated revenue impact, a specific suggested price, and a confidence score.</p>
          <div class="tc-stats">
            <div class="tc-stat"><span class="tc-stat-lbl">Detection</span><span class="tc-stat-val" style="color:var(--grn-txt)">Real-time</span></div>
            <div class="tc-stat"><span class="tc-stat-lbl">Platforms</span><span class="tc-stat-val">Amazon · Shopify · Woo</span></div>
            <div class="tc-stat"><span class="tc-stat-lbl">Output</span><span class="tc-stat-val" style="color:var(--grn-txt)">Decision, not data</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="tc-pc">
            <div class="pc-col">
              <span class="pc-lbl pc-lbl-g">Strengths</span>
              <div class="pc-item"><span class="dot-g">✓</span>Alerts the moment a competitor changes price</div>
              <div class="pc-item"><span class="dot-g">✓</span>Shows exact revenue loss per day at current price</div>
              <div class="pc-item"><span class="dot-g">✓</span>Gives a specific price target, not a vague direction</div>
              <div class="pc-item"><span class="dot-g">✓</span>Explains the likely reason behind the change</div>
              <div class="pc-item"><span class="dot-g">✓</span>Works across Amazon, Shopify, WooCommerce</div>
            </div>
            <div class="pc-col">
              <span class="pc-lbl pc-lbl-r">Limitations</span>
              <div class="pc-item"><span class="dot-r">✗</span>Newer product — smaller historical dataset than Keepa</div>
              <div class="pc-item"><span class="dot-r">✗</span>Not optimized for passive reporting workflows</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="callout callout-green">
        <p><strong>Example alert:</strong> "NikeStore dropped Air Force 1 by 12% — you're losing <strong>$320/day</strong> at current price. Drop to $109 to recover position #2. You'll still be $4 above the cheapest option." That's the difference between a tracker and a decision engine.</p>
      </div>

      <hr/>

      <h2 id="keepa">2. Keepa — Best for historical research</h2>
      <div class="tool-card">
        <div class="tc-head">
          <div class="tc-head-left"><span class="tc-rank">#2</span><div class="tc-name">Keepa</div><div class="tc-tagline">The most comprehensive Amazon price history database available.</div></div>
          <div class="tc-verdict-wrap"><span class="verdict-lbl">Verdict</span><span class="v-badge vb-ok">Research only</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="tc-content">
          <p class="tc-desc">Keepa has the deepest Amazon price history. For sourcing decisions, competitive research, or understanding seasonal patterns, it's unmatched. But it's backward-looking — tells you what happened, not what to do now.</p>
          <div class="tc-pc">
            <div class="pc-col"><span class="pc-lbl pc-lbl-g">Strengths</span>
              <div class="pc-item"><span class="dot-g">✓</span>Years of historical price data per ASIN</div>
              <div class="pc-item"><span class="dot-g">✓</span>Reliable, accurate tracking</div>
              <div class="pc-item"><span class="dot-g">✓</span>Free tier available</div>
            </div>
            <div class="pc-col"><span class="pc-lbl pc-lbl-r">Limitations</span>
              <div class="pc-item"><span class="dot-r">✗</span>No real-time alerts</div>
              <div class="pc-item"><span class="dot-r">✗</span>No suggested actions or impact estimates</div>
              <div class="pc-item"><span class="dot-r">✗</span>Amazon-only — no cross-platform</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p>Use Keepa when you need: <em>"What has this product's price done historically?"</em> Don't rely on it for: <em>"What should I do right now?"</em></p>

      <hr/>

      <h2 id="camel">3. CamelCamelCamel — Free, basic, slow</h2>
      <div class="tool-card">
        <div class="tc-head">
          <div class="tc-head-left"><span class="tc-rank">#3</span><div class="tc-name">CamelCamelCamel</div><div class="tc-tagline">Simple, free Amazon price history — for casual shoppers, not sellers.</div></div>
          <div class="tc-verdict-wrap"><span class="verdict-lbl">Verdict</span><span class="v-badge vb-limited">Casual use only</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="tc-content">
          <p class="tc-desc">Free consumer-grade tool built to help shoppers find deals. Simple, accessible, and completely unsuitable for active sellers who need speed and decision support.</p>
          <div class="tc-cons-list">
            <span class="tc-cons-lbl">Key limitations</span>
            <div class="con-item"><span class="con-dot">✗</span>Data is significantly delayed</div>
            <div class="con-item"><span class="con-dot">✗</span>No automation, no integrations, no API</div>
            <div class="con-item"><span class="con-dot">✗</span>No decision support — just raw charts</div>
            <div class="con-item"><span class="con-dot">✗</span>Built for shoppers, not sellers</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="parasite-section">
        <h3>Is CamelCamelCamel enough for sellers?</h3>
        <p>CamelCamelCamel is great for shoppers looking for deal alerts. But for sellers who need to track competitor prices and react in real time, it falls short.</p>
        <p>It shows you history — not what to do next. That's the gap for serious Amazon sellers.</p>
      </div>

      <hr/>

      <h2 id="repricer">4. RepricerExpress — Automation without intelligence</h2>
      <div class="tool-card">
        <div class="tc-head">
          <div class="tc-head-left"><span class="tc-rank">#4</span><div class="tc-name">RepricerExpress</div><div class="tc-tagline">Rule-based repricing automation for Amazon sellers.</div></div>
          <div class="tc-verdict-wrap"><span class="verdict-lbl">Verdict</span><span class="v-badge vb-ok">Rules, not reasoning</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="tc-content">
          <p class="tc-desc">Automates price changes based on rules you set. It reacts faster than humans — but operates entirely on logic you define. No AI reasoning, no impact estimation, no understanding of <em>why</em> a competitor moved.</p>
          <div class="tc-pc">
            <div class="pc-col"><span class="pc-lbl pc-lbl-g">Strengths</span>
              <div class="pc-item"><span class="dot-g">✓</span>Fast automated repricing</div>
              <div class="pc-item"><span class="dot-g">✓</span>Useful for high-volume sellers</div>
            </div>
            <div class="pc-col"><span class="pc-lbl pc-lbl-r">Limitations</span>
              <div class="pc-item"><span class="dot-r">✗</span>Rules-only — can trigger price wars</div>
              <div class="pc-item"><span class="dot-r">✗</span>No reasoning behind decisions</div>
              <div class="pc-item"><span class="dot-r">✗</span>No revenue impact visibility</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="callout callout-red">
        <p>⚠️ <strong>The race-to-the-bottom risk:</strong> Rule-based repricers trigger automated price wars. Without understanding <em>why</em> a competitor moved, automation can destroy margin faster than inaction.</p>
      </div>

      <hr/>

      <h2 id="sellersnap">5. SellerSnap — AI repricing, complex setup</h2>
      <div class="tool-card">
        <div class="tc-head">
          <div class="tc-head-left"><span class="tc-rank">#5</span><div class="tc-name">SellerSnap</div><div class="tc-tagline">Game-theory AI repricing for advanced Amazon sellers.</div></div>
          <div class="tc-verdict-wrap"><span class="verdict-lbl">Verdict</span><span class="v-badge vb-limited">Complex to deploy</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="tc-content">
          <p class="tc-desc">Applies game-theory models to repricing, trying to avoid race-to-bottom. More sophisticated than rules — but expensive, hard to configure, and still doesn't explain its reasoning.</p>
          <div class="tc-cons-list">
            <span class="tc-cons-lbl">Key limitations</span>
            <div class="con-item"><span class="con-dot">✗</span>High price point</div>
            <div class="con-item"><span class="con-dot">✗</span>Complex configuration</div>
            <div class="con-item"><span class="con-dot">✗</span>Black-box decisions</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <hr/>

      <h2 id="buybox">Why the Buy Box changes everything</h2>
      <p>The Buy Box is the "Add to Cart" button. <strong>82% of Amazon sales go through it.</strong> Losing it doesn't mean you sell less — you sell almost nothing, even if your listing is live.</p>

      <div class="buybox-block">
        <div class="bb-scenario">
          <div class="bb-label">Without real-time intelligence</div>
          <div class="bb-step"><span class="bb-num">1.</span><span>Competitor drops price by 5% at 9:14 AM</span></div>
          <div class="bb-step"><span class="bb-num">2.</span><span><strong>You lose the Buy Box</strong></span></div>
          <div class="bb-step"><span class="bb-num">3.</span><span>You check sales at 4 PM</span></div>
          <div class="bb-step"><span class="bb-num">4.</span><span>Lost sales for 7 hours without knowing</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="bb-scenario">
          <div class="bb-label">With Talon</div>
          <div class="bb-step"><span class="bb-num">1.</span><span>Competitor drops price at 9:14 AM</span></div>
          <div class="bb-step"><span class="bb-num">2.</span><span>Talon alerts at 9:15: <strong>$180/day</strong></span></div>
          <div class="bb-step"><span class="bb-num">3.</span><span>Suggested: drop to $43.50</span></div>
          <div class="bb-step"><span class="bb-num">4.</span><span><strong>You act in minutes</strong></span></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <hr/>

      <h2 id="why">Why most price tracking tools fail sellers</h2>
      <p>Every tool here does something useful. None — except Talon — closes the gap between raw data and the decision you need.</p>

      <div class="fail-grid">
        <div class="fail-cell">
          <div class="fail-cell-lbl fail-cell-lbl-r">What most give you</div>
          <div class="fail-item"><span class="fail-arrow">→</span>"Competitor dropped price 8%"</div>
          <div class="fail-item"><span class="fail-arrow">→</span>A chart over 30 days</div>
          <div class="fail-item"><span class="fail-arrow">→</span>Weekly report</div>
        </div>
        <div class="fail-cell">
          <div class="fail-cell-lbl fail-cell-lbl-g">What you actually need</div>
          <div class="fail-item"><span class="fail-arrow">→</span>Should I react or wait?</div>
          <div class="fail-item"><span class="fail-arrow">→</span>How much am I losing per day?</div>
          <div class="fail-item"><span class="fail-arrow">→</span>What exact price recovers position?</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <hr/>

      <h2 id="who">Who should use which tool</h2>

      <div class="who-grid">
        <div class="who-card">
          <span class="who-tag">Casual seller</span>
          <div class="who-title">CamelCamelCamel or Keepa</div>
          <div class="who-desc">If you sell a handful of products and check weekly, free tools are fine.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="who-card">
          <span class="who-tag">Research-heavy sourcer</span>
          <div class="who-title">Keepa</div>
          <div class="who-desc">Wholesale arbitrage sellers who need deep historical data before buying.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="who-card">
          <span class="who-tag">High-volume catalog</span>
          <div class="who-title">RepricerExpress</div>
          <div class="who-desc">500+ SKUs needing automated repricing.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="who-card">
          <span class="who-tag">Active — margin matters</span>
          <div class="who-title">Talon</div>
          <div class="who-tool-best">Best for real-time</div>
          <div class="who-desc">React fast, protect margin, understand <em>why</em> — not just what.</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <hr/>

      <h2 id="takeaway">Final takeaway</h2>
      <p>Tracking prices is table stakes. The question isn't <em>whether</em> you track — it's what happens in the 15 minutes after a competitor moves.</p>
      <p><strong>If you're an active seller who needs to protect the Buy Box, capture margin windows, and understand <em>why</em> competitors are moving — Talon is the only tool built for that workflow.</strong></p>
      <p>Winning on Amazon is about reacting faster than your competitors.</p>

      <div class="article-cta">
        <div class="cta-left">
          <span class="cta-eyebrow">Free analysis — no signup</span>
          <div class="cta-title">See if you're losing the Buy Box right now</div>
          <div class="cta-sub">Paste your ASIN and a competitor. Get real-time impact and price in seconds.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="cta-right">
          <a href="/#tool" class="cta-btn">→ Start free analysis</a>
          <span class="cta-note">No account · No credit card</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div slot="sidebar">
      <div class="sidebar-cta">
        <span class="sb-title">Losing the Buy Box?</span>
        <div class="sb-desc">Paste your product and competitor. Get estimated impact and price in seconds.</div>
        <a href="/#tool" class="sb-btn">→ Analyze your product</a>
        <span class="sb-note">No signup · No credit card</span>
      </div>

      <div class="sidebar-toc">
        <div class="sidebar-lbl">In this article</div>
        <ul class="toc-list">
          <li class="toc-item"><a href="#comparison"><span class="toc-num">01</span>Quick comparison</a></li>
          <li class="toc-item"><a href="#talon"><span class="toc-num">02</span>Talon</a></li>
          <li class="toc-item"><a href="#keepa"><span class="toc-num">03</span>Keepa</a></li>
          <li class="toc-item"><a href="#camel"><span class="toc-num">04</span>CamelCamelCamel</a></li>
          <li class="toc-item"><a href="#repricer"><span class="toc-num">05</span>RepricerExpress</a></li>
          <li class="toc-item"><a href="#sellersnap"><span class="toc-num">06</span>SellerSnap</a></li>
          <li class="toc-item"><a href="#buybox"><span class="toc-num">07</span>Buy Box problem</a></li>
          <li class="toc-item"><a href="#why"><span class="toc-num">08</span>Why tools fail</a></li>
          <li class="toc-item"><a href="#who"><span class="toc-num">09</span>Who uses what</a></li>
          <li class="toc-item"><a href="#takeaway"><span class="toc-num">10</span>Final takeaway</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="sidebar-related">
        <div class="sidebar-lbl">Related articles</div>
        <div class="related-list">
          <div class="related-item"><span class="rel-cat">Tools</span><a href="/best-competitor-price-tracking-tools" class="rel-title">Best Competitor Price Tracking Tools</a></div>
          <div class="related-item"><span class="rel-cat">Platform</span><a href="/shopify-competitor-price-monitoring" class="rel-title">Shopify Price Monitoring</a></div>
          <div class="related-item"><span class="rel-cat">Problem</span><a href="/why-your-product-is-not-selling" class="rel-title">Why Your Product Is Not Selling</a></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </BlogPost>
</Layout>

<style>
.prose{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0}
.prose h2{font-family:var(--display);font-size:24px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-0.4px;color:var(--t1);margin:48px 0 16px;line-height:1.25;scroll-margin-top:80px}
.prose p{color:var(--t2);margin-bottom:18px;font-size:var(--body-size);line-height:var(--body-lh)}
.prose strong{color:var(--t1);font-weight:600}
.prose hr{border:none;border-top:1px solid var(--border);margin:40px 0}

.lead{font-size:19px;color:var(--t2);line-height:1.65;margin-bottom:24px}

.stat-trio{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:1px;background:var(--border);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;margin:0 0 40px}
.stat-item{background:var(--bg1);padding:20px 22px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px}
.stat-num{font-family:var(--display);font-size:28px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-0.6px;line-height:1}
.stat-num-r{color:var(--red-txt)}
.stat-num-g{color:var(--grn-txt)}
.stat-num-w{color:var(--t1)}
.stat-label{font-size:12.5px;color:var(--t2);line-height:1.4}
.stat-sub{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;color:var(--t3);letter-spacing:0.2px}

.comparison-wrap{overflow-x:auto;margin:0 0 40px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:10px}
.comparison-table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:14px}
.comparison-table thead tr{background:var(--bg2)}
.comparison-table th{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px;color:var(--t3);padding:12px 18px;text-align:left}
.comparison-table tbody tr{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}
.comparison-table td{padding:13px 18px;color:var(--t2)}
.comparison-table td:first-child{color:var(--t1);font-weight:500}
.hl{background:var(--bg2)}
.tc-icon{margin-right:6px}
.tc-us-chip{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;padding:2px 7px;border-radius:10px;background:var(--amb-lo);color:var(--amb-txt);border:1px solid var(--amb-bd)}
.check-yes{color:var(--grn-txt)}
.check-warn{color:var(--amb-txt)}
.check-no{color:var(--t3)}

.tool-card{border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;margin:28px 0;background:var(--bg1)}
.tool-card.featured{border-color:var(--border-md);background:var(--bg2)}
.tc-head{padding:22px 24px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:16px}
.tc-head-left{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:5px}
.tc-rank{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;color:var(--t3);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px}
.tc-name{font-family:var(--display);font-size:21px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-0.3px;color:var(--t1)}
.tc-tagline{font-size:13.5px;color:var(--t2);margin-top:2px}
.tc-verdict-wrap{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-end;gap:4px}
.verdict-lbl{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:9px;color:var(--t3);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.8px}
.v-badge{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;font-weight:500;padding:4px 11px;border-radius:5px}
.vb-best{background:var(--grn-lo);color:var(--grn-txt);border:1px solid var(--grn-bd)}
.vb-ok{background:var(--amb-lo);color:var(--amb-txt);border:1px solid var(--amb-bd)}
.vb-limited{background:var(--bg3);color:var(--t3);border:1px solid var(--border)}
.tc-content{padding:22px 24px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px}
.tc-desc{font-size:14.5px;color:var(--t2);line-height:1.65}

.tc-stats{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:1px;background:var(--border);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px}
.tc-stat{background:var(--bg3);padding:12px 14px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px}
.tc-stat-lbl{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;color:var(--t3);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.8px}
.tc-stat-val{font-size:13.5px;font-weight:500;color:var(--t1)}

.tc-pc{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:12px}
.pc-col{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px}
.pc-lbl{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.8px;margin-bottom:2px}
.pc-lbl-g{color:var(--grn-txt)}
.pc-lbl-r{color:var(--red-txt)}
.pc-item{display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:7px;font-size:13px;color:var(--t2);line-height:1.5}
.dot-g{color:var(--grn-txt);font-size:11px;margin-top:3px}
.dot-r{color:var(--red-txt);font-size:11px;margin-top:3px}

.tc-cons-list{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px}
.tc-cons-lbl{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;color:var(--t3);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.8px}
.con-item{display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:8px;font-size:13.5px;color:var(--t2)}
.con-dot{color:var(--red-txt);font-size:11px;margin-top:3px}

.callout{background:var(--bg2);border:1px solid var(--border-md);border-left:3px solid var(--amb-txt);border-radius:0 8px 8px 0;padding:16px 20px;margin:24px 0}
.callout p{color:var(--t2);font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;margin:0}
.callout strong{color:var(--t1)}
.callout-green{border-left-color:var(--grn-txt)}
.callout-red{border-left-color:var(--red-txt)}

.buybox-block{background:var(--bg2);border:1px solid var(--border-md);border-radius:12px;padding:28px 32px;margin:32px 0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:24px}
.bb-label{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px;color:var(--t3);margin-bottom:12px}
.bb-scenario{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px}
.bb-step{display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:10px;font-size:14px;color:var(--t2);line-height:1.5}
.bb-num{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;color:var(--t3);flex-shrink:0;margin-top:2px;width:18px}

.fail-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:2px;background:var(--border);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;margin:24px 0}
.fail-cell{background:var(--bg2);padding:24px 26px}
.fail-cell-lbl{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px;margin-bottom:14px}
.fail-cell-lbl-r{color:var(--red-txt)}
.fail-cell-lbl-g{color:var(--grn-txt)}
.fail-item{display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:9px;font-size:14px;color:var(--t2);margin-bottom:10px}
.fail-arrow{color:var(--t3);flex-shrink:0}

.who-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:10px;margin:24px 0}
.who-card{background:var(--bg2);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:10px;padding:18px 20px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px}
.who-tag{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;color:var(--t3);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.8px}
.who-title{font-size:14px;font-weight:600;color:var(--t1)}
.who-tool-best{color:var(--grn-txt);font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px}
.who-desc{font-size:12.5px;color:var(--t2);line-height:1.5}

.article-cta{background:var(--bg2);border:1px solid var(--border-md);border-radius:12px;padding:36px 40px;margin:48px 0 0;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:32px}
.cta-left{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px;flex:1}
.cta-eyebrow{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;color:var(--t3);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px}
.cta-title{font-family:var(--display);font-size:22px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-0.4px;color:var(--t1);line-height:1.2}
.cta-sub{font-size:14px;color:var(--t2);line-height:1.5}
.cta-right{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-end;gap:8px}
.cta-btn{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;padding:13px 24px;background:var(--t1);color:var(--bg0);border:none;border-radius:8px;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none}
.cta-note{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;color:var(--t3)}

.sidebar-cta{background:var(--bg2);border:1px solid var(--border-md);border-radius:10px;padding:18px 20px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:10px}
.sb-title{font-family:var(--display);font-size:16px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.2px;color:var(--t1)}
.sb-desc{font-size:12.5px;color:var(--t2);line-height:1.55}
.sb-btn{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:6px;padding:11px;background:var(--t1);color:var(--bg0);border:none;border-radius:7px;font-size:13px;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none}
.sb-note{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;color:var(--t3);text-align:center}

.sidebar-toc{background:var(--bg1);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:10px;padding:18px 20px}
.sidebar-lbl{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px;color:var(--t3);margin-bottom:14px}
.toc-list{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;list-style:none}
.toc-item a{display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:8px;font-size:12.5px;color:var(--t3);text-decoration:none;padding:5px 0;line-height:1.45}
.toc-item a:hover{color:var(--t2)}
.toc-num{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;flex-shrink:0;margin-top:2px}

.sidebar-related{background:var(--bg1);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:10px;padding:18px 20px}
.related-list{display:flex;flex-direction:column}
.related-item{padding:10px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}
.rel-cat{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:9.5px;color:var(--t3);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.8px}
.rel-title{font-size:13px;color:var(--t2);text-decoration:none;display:block;margin-top:4px}
.rel-title:hover{color:var(--t1)}
</style>

<script>
const sections = document.querySelectorAll('h2[id]');
const tocLinks = document.querySelectorAll('.toc-item a');
const observer = new IntersectionObserver(entries => {
  entries.forEach(entry => {
    if (entry.isIntersecting) {
      const id = entry.target.getAttribute('id');
      tocLinks.forEach(l => l.classList.toggle('active-toc', l.getAttribute('href') === '#' + id));
    }
  });
}, { rootMargin: '-20% 0px -70% 0px' });
sections.forEach(s => observer.observe(s));
</script>